# Core lexicon: general vocabulary of everyday life and of modern subjects, sorted by keyword.
# A row with q is a draft that no speaker of the language has confirmed yet.
ahih hangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but) (d:ahih, being so, with hangin, although: although that is so; joins two statements that contrast) (r:1.6.8)
ahihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if) (d:ahih, being so, with leh, if: if it is, if he is, after a noun or a clause) (s:hileh)
ak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/food) (w:chicken/fowl/rooster) (d:the domestic fowl, a chicken; ak a khuang is the rooster crows) (s:aak/aklui) (q:draft)
aktui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:egg) (d:the egg of a hen) (s:tuii) (q:draft)
amah = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/she) (d:third person singular pronoun used of a person, man or woman) (r:zai:he) (q:draft)
amau = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:those/they/their/them) (d:Third person plural pronoun, they or them; before a noun, often written amau’ with an apostrophe, it means their.) (s:amaute)
amaute = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:they) (d:Third person plural pronoun, amau with the plural te; as the subject it is usually followed by in.) (b:amau)
an = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food) (d:Food in general, and also grain or a meal.) (s:nektawm)
anbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:kitchen) (d:an, food, with buk, hut or shelter: a place where food is cooked) (q:draft)
anhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:cook/prepare food) (d:cook food, prepare a meal. From an, food, with huan, cook) (r:1.40.1) (q:draft)
anlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:harvest/reaping) (d:the gathering in of the grain; anlak hun is harvest time and anlak na sem is work at the harvest) (s:atna) (r:41.12.2) (q:draft)
annekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:meal/eating) (d:annek, eat food, with the noun suffix na: the eating of a meal; annekna sabuai is the table for a meal and annekna mun a banquet hall) (s:nekna/anneek) (b:annek) (r:17.7.8) (q:draft)
anteh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:vegetable/greens) (d:leafy plants eaten as food; anteh huan is a vegetable garden) (s:mehteh) (r:20.15.17) (q:draft)
at = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:cut) (d:cut with a blade. At khia is cut off) (q:draft)
at = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:reap/harvest) (d:cut grain at harvest; buh at is to reap the grain, and at is set against vawh, sow) (s:anla) (a:vawh/tuh) (q:draft)
aw = (i:3) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:yes) (d:answer of agreement to a question or an invitation) (s:awleh)
awleh = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:yes) (s:aw)
baih = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:early/soon/quickly) (d:placed after a verb: early, soon or quickly; tho baih is rise early) (s:tungin/pak) (q:draft)
baih = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy) (d:not hard to do; baih zaw means easier) (s:ol) (a:haksa/hak) (q:draft)
bang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:what) (d:Question word, what; it also begins the phrases bang hangin, why, and bang ci, how.) (r:44.21.22)
bang hang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:why) (d:asks the reason, often as bang hang hiam) (r:zai:why) (q:draft)
bangci = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how) (d:Question word, how, in what way; also with the ending in, bangci-in.) (s:koici)
bangcia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why) for what reason or purpose
bangzah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how many/how much) (d:Asks or exclaims about amount or degree, how much or how many; bangzah takin sang is how high) (q:draft)
bawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make/create) (d:make or form something from material, or bring it into being; thuciamna bawl is make a covenant) (s:piang/Piangsak) (a:susia)
bawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:basket/cage) (d:a container made to hold things, such as a basket of fruit or a cage for birds and animals) (s:seeng) (r:26.19.9) (q:draft)
bawng = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/food) (w:cow/ox/cattle) (d:cow or ox, the general word for cattle of either sex; bawngpi is the female, bawngtal the male and bawngno the young)
bawngnawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:milk) (d:the milk of a cow) (s:nawi) (q:draft)
beel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:pot/jar/vessel) (d:container of clay, metal, wood or stone used for cooking, for storing things or for carrying water; beel kitam is a broken pot, a potsherd) (r:24.19.10) (q:draft)
beh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family) (d:group of related families within a tribe) (s:phung) (r:15.10.38) (q:draft)
bek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/alone) (d:placed after the word it limits: that one and no other, that much and no more) (s:lel) (q:draft)
biakinn = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:church/church building) (d:a house of worship, the building where a congregation meets) (r:zai:church) (q:draft)
buh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food) (w:rice) (d:rice as a plant and as grain) (r:zai:rice) (q:draft)
ci = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/tell) (d:say; stands after the words quoted, as in a ci hi, he said, and ci-in, saying) (r:1.21.24)
ci = (i:4) (t:n) (f:food) (w:salt) (r:zai:salt) (q:draft)
ciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go home/go back) (d:go back to one's home or to the place one came from) (s:ciahkik/paikik/kilehkik) (r:40.9.7)
ciahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:Ciah, return, with kik, back or again: go or come back to where one was.) (s:ciah/paikik/kilehkik) (b:ciah) (r:1.3.19)
ciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:promise/swear/vow) (d:Give one’s word or swear an oath; often with thu, as in thu ciam, make a promise on oath) (s:kiciam/kamciam) (q:draft)
ciangin = (i:3) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:and/when) (d:joins a clause to what follows: when or after this happened, and then) as in Let there be light, and there was light"
cidam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/everyday) (w:healthy/well) (d:in good health; cidam lo is sick) (a:cina) (q:draft)
cik = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:when) (d:Question word of time, used in cik ciangin, when, at what time) (s:cikciangin/cikciang/cikin) (r:19.42.2) (q:draft)
cikmah = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never) (d:With hun or ciangin and a negative verb: at no time, never.) (s:cikmahin/cik)
cina = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/everyday) (w:sick/ill) (d:Sick, ill; also used as a verb, be ill or fall sick, often as cina-in om) (a:cidam) (r:25.5.17) (q:draft)
dah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:mourn/grieve/be sad) (d:feel sorrow, above all over a death or a loss; the opposite of lungdam, be glad) (a:lungdam/kipak) (r:1.27.41)
dai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:quiet/calm/silent/still) (d:without noise or movement, of people, wind or sea; also as a verb, be quiet, fall silent, die down; dai takin is quietly, dai dide utterly still) (s:daii/gamdai/daicip) (r:19.107.29) (q:draft)
dam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be well/be healed/recover) (d:be in good health or get well again; of a sickness, wound or sorrow, heal; na dam hiam, are you well, is a greeting) (a:nat) (r:24.8.18) (q:draft)
dangtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food/body) (w:thirsty) (d:be thirsty, often paired with gilkial, hungry; also thirst) (s:tuiduh/duh) (r:20.25.25) (q:draft)
dawl = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:floor) (d:a floor or storey of a building)
dawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:meet/welcome/go to meet) (d:go out to meet someone who is coming) (s:dawntuah/kimu) (q:draft)
dawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:drink) (d:take a drink; tui dawn is to drink water and zu dawn to drink wine or beer) (q:draft)
dawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:answer/reply) (d:give an answer to a person or to a question) (s:dawngkik) (a:dong/dot) (r:24.21.3) (q:draft)
dei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:room/chamber) (d:a room of a house or building; dei tungnung is an upstairs room) (s:inndei/adei) (r:44.20.8)
deih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want/desire/wish) (d:wish to have something or wish that something happens; the thing or clause wanted comes before it) (s:lunggulh)
deih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:like/love) (d:be fond of or take pleasure in someone or something) (s:lunggulh) (a:mudah/hua)
den = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:always/continually/constantly) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing, or remain so without change) (s:niloh/ngitnget/gige) (r:19.7.11) (q:draft)
dik = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:right/correct/just/honest) (d:right or correct, as it ought to be; of a person upright and honest) (s:thuman/thutang) (a:gilo/thumanlo) (r:19.11.7) (q:draft)
dim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:full) (d:holding as much as there is room for; with tawh it says what something is full of) (a:awng/hawm/hawmguak)
ding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:stand) (r:zai:stand) (q:draft)
dong = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask/inquire/question) (d:put a question to someone or seek advice; the form dot is used in dependent clauses) (s:thudong/kan) (a:dawng) (q:draft)
dum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:blue) (d:the colour blue, said of cloth and cord; the same word is used of green plants) (q:draft)
eite = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:we/us/our) (d:first person plural including the hearer; whether English has we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (s:eimau) (b:ei) (r:58.10.15)
en = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:look/see/behold) (d:look at someone or something; the commands en in, to one person, and en un, to several, are often rendered behold) (s:khuadak/dak) (r:1.1.31)
eng = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:yellow) (d:yellow in colour; mul eng is yellow hair) (q:draft)
etlawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:lovely/beautiful/fair) (d:pleasant to look at; et, look, with lawm, fitting) (s:melhoih/meelhoih/ngaihhuai) (a:melsia) (q:draft)
gah = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:fruit/crop/produce) (d:The fruit or crop that a tree, plant or field bears; also the result of work or conduct.) (s:singgah)
gam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:country) (d:A country or region with its people; mualtung gam is hill country.)
gamla = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:far/distant/far away) (d:far in place; with a before it and panin or ah after it, it is used as a noun: a gamla panin is from a distance, a gamla-ah is at a distance) (a:kinai) (r:41.5.6) (q:draft)
gelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:write) (d:put words down in letters. With lai, writing, it means write a letter or a document) (s:at/laigelh) (a:phiat) (q:draft)
gen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell/say/speak) (d:say or tell something in words; the basic verb of speaking, as in thu gen, speak a word) (s:ci)
gik = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:heavy/weighing) (d:heavy, having much weight; after an amount it gives the weight) (r:14.4.18) (q:draft)
gilkial = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food/body) (w:hungry) (d:feeling the need of food; from gil, belly, and kial, be hungry) (r:19.107.5)
gim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:tire/be tired/be weary) (d:be tired or worn out from effort; gim also stands for suffering in gim thuak, suffer, and gim pia, punish) (s:tawl)
gol = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:big/large/thick) (d:big, large or thick in size; gol zaw is bigger and a gol mahmah is very big) (s:lian/lianpi) (a:neu) (q:draft)
guak = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:only) (d:no more than, placed after the word it limits: khat guak is only one)
guak = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:alone) (d:by oneself, with no one else; follows a pronoun or a name, as amah guak, he alone) (s:guakbek/khatguak)
hai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:cup/bowl) (d:a cup to drink from, or a small bowl) (q:draft)
haksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:hard/difficult) (d:Hard to do, to bear or to understand; nasep haksa is hard labour, and thu-haksa is a riddle or hard saying) (s:hak) (a:baih/ol) (q:draft)
hanciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:make an effort to do or reach something; it often follows a purpose clause with dingin or nadingin) (s:hahkat/hamciam) (r:20.2.2) (q:draft)
hat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:strong/mighty/powerful) (d:strong, said of a person, an arm, an enemy, the wind or a city; often with tha, strength, as in a tha hat, his strength is great; after a verb it means do something fast or much, as in tai hat, run fast) (s:thahat/vanglian) (a:thanem) (r:19.24.8) (q:draft)
hau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:rich/wealthy) (d:rich, or as a verb be rich; after a noun it means have much of it, as in sum hau, rich in money) (s:sumhau) (a:zawng) (q:draft)
hawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:visit/call on/go to see) (d:go to see a person or a place) (s:veh) (q:draft)
hawm = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:empty/hollow) (d:with nothing inside: empty or hollow, and of ears of grain thin; khut hawm guak is empty-handed) (s:awng/hawmguak) (a:dim) (q:draft)
hawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:divide/distribute/share) (d:give each person a part of something: divide land, goods or spoil among people, or share what one has with others) (s:khen/sehkhen) (r:45.12.13) (q:draft)
heh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:angry) (d:feeling anger; the person one is angry with is followed by tungah)
hi mah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:yes) (d:it is so, said in agreement) (r:zai:yes) (q:draft)
hiah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:here) (d:in or at this place; Hiah om ing, here I am, is the answer of someone who is called) (s:hihlai-ah) (a:tuasan)
hiam = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:sharp) (d:having a keen edge, of a knife or blade; the opposite of mawl, blunt) (r:zai:bluntness) (q:draft, low confidence)
hih = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:points to a person or thing near the speaker or just mentioned; before a noun it means this or these, and hih bangin is in this way) (a:tua) (r:43.8.4)
hih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do) (r:zai:do) (q:draft)
hihnu = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:she/her/this woman) (d:hih, this, with nu marking a woman: this woman, she, said of a woman who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuanu)
hihpa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/him/this man) (d:hih, this, with pa marking a man: this man, he, said of a man who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuapa) (r:1.5.29)
hilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:teach/instruct) (d:teach or instruct someone, show how a thing is done) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (a:sin) (q:draft)
hilo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not/no) (d:is not, the negative of hi, be, written as one word; as a reply it means no, it is not so) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good/fine) (d:good in quality or in character, also fine or beautiful; hoih lo is not good) (s:pha) (a:gilo/hoihlo/siat) (r:25.3.25)
hoihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:bad/not good) (d:hoih, good, with the negative lo, written as one word: not good, bad) (s:gilo/siat) (a:hoih) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
hon = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open) (d:open a door, a gate, a book or the eyes; before sak it is written with an apostrophe) (a:khaksak/kalh) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft)
hopihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:greeting/salutation) (d:words spoken to greet someone) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hua = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:that/yonder/that over there) (d:points to something far from both speaker and hearer; hua lai-ah and hua lamah mean over there, in contrast with hih, this) (s:hia) (r:19.104.26) (q:draft)
huan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:cook) (r:zai:cook) (q:draft)
huh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help) (d:do something for someone so that things go better for them; hong huh in is the cry help me) (s:panpih) (a:nawngkaisak) (r:19.118.13)
hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/period/season) (d:a point or stretch of time; tua hun lai takin means at that time, and hun sung means during a period)
ihmu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:sleep) (a:khanglo/khanlawh)
inn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:home/house) (s:innsung/teenna)
inndei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:room) (d:a room in a house or other building; lupna inndei is a bedroom) (s:dei) (r:11.6.30) (q:draft)
innkhum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:roof) (d:the top of a house; innkhum zang is the flat roof, innkhum dawn the rooftop) (s:khum/innkhumzang/tungkhum) (q:draft)
innkuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:family) (d:the people of one house and line, parents and children together) (s:innkuanpih)
innsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/family) (w:home/household) (d:inn, house, with sung, inside: the inside of a house, and so the home and the people who live in it) (s:innkuan/innkuansung) (q:draft)
innveng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:neighbourhood/neighbour) (d:the houses near one's own and those who live there) (s:veng) (q:draft)
it = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family/social) (w:love/hold dear) (d:love a person or a thing, hold dear) (a:mudah/hua) (r:59.1.16) (q:draft)
itna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family/social) (w:love) (d:the feeling of love for a person, from it, love, with the noun suffix na) (a:muhdahna) (b:it) (r:65.1.2) (q:draft)
ka = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:my) (d:first person singular possessive placed before a noun)
kah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:climb/go up/ascend) (d:go up onto a hill, a wall, a ladder or a boat) (s:kahto/paito) (a:kumsuk/paisuk/kahsuk) (q:draft)
kahto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go up/ascend/climb/rise) (d:kah, climb, with to, upward: go or climb up to a higher place, as a mountain, a ship or heaven; also of smoke rising) (s:paito) (a:kahsuk/kumsuk/paisuk) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull/draw/drag) (d:draw something toward oneself or along behind) (q:draft)
kalsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:walk/step/take a step) (d:move forward on foot, take steps) (r:45.8.1) (q:draft)
kamciam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:pledge/promise/vow) (d:a promise given by word of mouth; kam, mouth, with ciam, promise) (s:kamciamna/thuciam/kiciamna) (q:draft)
kammal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:word/speech) (d:kam, mouth, with mal, a single unit: a word, a thing said) (s:kamgen) (r:21.12.10) (q:draft)
kampau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:language/speech/words) (d:kam, mouth, with pau, speak: the language a people speaks, or what a person says) (s:pau/kammal) (r:20.12.25) (q:draft)
kang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:white) (d:white in colour, said of a horse, of hair or of a patch of skin; also written kaang) (s:kaang) (a:vom) (q:draft)
kap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:weep/cry/mourn) (d:shed tears: weep, cry or mourn for someone; nakpi-in kap is weep bitterly) (s:kah/thuum) (a:nui) (r:43.11.35) (q:draft)
kawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:wall) (d:the wall of a house or room; kawm bangin is like a wall) (q:draft)
kawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:wet/be wet) (d:be or become wet or moist; of water, soak the ground or a thing) (a:keu)
kei = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:I/me) (d:first person singular pronoun: I or me; with the possessive mark it means my) (s:ken/ke)
kei = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:do not/shall not/will not/not) (d:negative word placed after the verb: kei hi states that something is not so, kei in and kei un forbid, and kei ding hi means shall not) (r:1.2.17)
keima = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:my/mine) (d:possessive form of kei, placed before a noun: my; keima aa means mine) (s:kei/ken) (b:kei)
ken = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:I) (s:kei)
keng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:take along/carry/bring) (d:have a thing with one on a journey, take or bring it along) (s:pua) (q:draft)
keu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:dry/dry up/wither) (d:be or become dry, said of water, land and plants; lei keu is dry land) (s:kang) (a:kawt)
kha = (i:3) (t:n) (f:time) (w:month) (d:a month of the year; kha khat is one month and kha masa the first month) (r:2.13.4)
kha = (i:5) (t:adj) (f:food/everyday) (w:bitter) (d:bitter in taste) (r:zai:bitter) (q:draft)
khak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:shut/close) (r:zai:shut) (q:draft)
khanglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:awake/wake up) (d:wake from sleep; khanglo in is the call to wake up) (s:khanlawh) (a:ihmu)
khangno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:young/youthful) (d:young in age; a khangno lai is while still young, and khangno mite are young people, the opposite of khangham mite) (s:moi/khangmoi) (a:khangham/teek) (r:18.33.25) (q:draft)
khangno = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:youth) (d:the time of being young, as in khangno lai) (s:khangnona/khangnolai) (q:draft)
khathei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:perhaps/maybe/probably) (d:placed after the verb to say that something may well happen or be so, often followed by ding) (q:draft)
khawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:along/together/side by side) (d:after a verb, doing the action together with others or jointly) (s:khawmin/khop)
khedap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:shoe/sandal) (d:footwear, a sandal or shoe; khedap bulh is put on sandals, khedap suah is take them off, and khedap khau is the sandal strap) (q:draft)
khempeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:every/all/everyone/everything) (d:all, every: placed after a noun, as mi khempeuh, all people or everyone, and thu khempeuh, everything)
khial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wrong/sin/do wrong/err) (d:do wrong or sin; with tungah, sin against someone) (s:mawh)
khin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:already) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is already done or complete) (s:khinta/khinzo) (a:nailo)
khomun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:bread/loaf) (d:bread or a loaf of bread) (s:anlum/moh/tangho) (q:draft)
khu = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:wear/put on) (d:put on or wear something on the head, such as a hat, crown or helmet) (q:draft)
khua = (i:4) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:seasonal/season) (d:the weather or time of year, in khua hun, season)
khua = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:village) (d:a village or small settlement, often said with neu, small, or no, little) (s:khuaneu)
khua = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:city/town) (d:a town or city, a place where many people live together; khua sung is inside the town and khua mite are its people) (s:khuapi)
khuakhal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:summer) (d:the hot, dry season of the year) (s:khualkhal) (a:phalbi) (q:draft)
khuaneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:village/small town) (d:khua, town, and neu, small; set against khuapi, city) (a:khuapi) (q:draft)
khuapi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:city/town) (d:a large town, khua, town, with pi, great) (a:khuaneu) (r:1.4.17)
khum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food/everyday) (w:sweet/pleasant) (d:sweet in taste; of speech pleasant or smooth, as in kam khum, sweet words) (q:draft)
kia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/drop) (d:fall down or drop from a height; said of a person, of rain and of seed that falls on the ground; the form kiat is used before leh and ciangin) (s:puk/tuk) (a:tho) (q:draft)
kibang = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:same/alike) (d:the same, not different; a kibang before a noun means the same, as in ngeina a kibang khat, one and the same law) (s:kikim) (a:tuam)
kicing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:enough/complete/full) (d:complete, perfect or enough; also used as a verb, be enough or be fulfilled, and a kicing lo is what is lacking) (s:cingtaak/kicingtaak) (q:draft)
kihong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open/be opened) (d:be open or be opened, said of a container, a door or gate, a tomb, the sky, and of eyes and ears; a kihong before a noun means open) (s:kihon) (a:kikhak) (r:40.27.52)
kik = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:again/back) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done again or turned back: gen kik is say again, pia kik is give back) (s:leuleu) (q:draft)
kikhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:meeting/assembly) (d:A gathering of people who come together, or the place where they gather) (s:kikaihkhopna) (r:4.16.43) (q:draft)
kilemna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:peace) (d:being on good terms after or instead of fighting, often as gal kilemna; kilemna bawl is make peace) (s:gallemna/galdaihna) (a:kidona/kilemlohna) (b:kilem) (q:draft)
kimawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:play) (d:Play, as children do; also perform or hold a contest for others to watch) (q:draft)
kimkhat = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:some/some of) (d:An indefinite number or part of a group or thing, placed after the noun; repeated, some and others; of a divided thing it can be one half.) (s:khenkhat/pawkhat)
kinai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be near/be close) (d:be near to a place or to each other, used with tawh; khat leh khat kinai, come near one another) (a:kigamla) (b:nai) (r:2.14.20) (q:draft)
kipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start) (d:start to do something or come into being; after a verb with ding, begin to do; with panin, start from a place) (s:kipat) (a:tawp/bei) (q:draft)
kisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:need/lack/be necessary/be needed) (d:be without something that is wanted or required: of a person, need or lack; of a thing, be needed or missing; ding kisam is it is necessary to) (s:kul/kiphamawh/tasam) (r:15.6.9) (q:draft)
kisik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:regret/repent) (d:feel sorry for something done and turn from it; mawhna kisik is repent of sin)
kisil = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:bathe/wash oneself) (d:sil, wash, with the reflexive prefix ki: wash oneself, bathe, or wash the hands before eating) (s:kipumsil) (b:sil) (q:draft)
kitenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:marriage/intermarriage) (d:kiten marry with the noun suffix na; kitenna bawl and kitenna nei are to marry) (s:kipina/tenpihna) (b:kiten) (q:draft)
kitot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:quarrel/dispute/strive/argue) (d:quarrel with one another; also used as a noun, a quarrel or strife) (s:kitawng/kinial/kisel/kiseel) (a:kilem/kithutuak) (q:draft)
kitotna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:strife/quarrel/conflict/dispute) (d:kitot quarrel with the noun suffix na: quarrelling and strife between people; kitotna piangsak is stir up strife) (s:kinialna/kiselna/kiseelna) (a:kilemna) (q:draft)
kituak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:match/agree/be consistent) (d:of statements, thoughts or minds: agree with one another, be the same; thu kituak lo is disagree) (s:kithutuak)
koi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:where) (d:question word for place, usually followed by a place word as in koi-ah, at what place, koi lai, whereabouts, and koi pan, from where) (s:koiah/koilai)
koizaw = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:which/which one) (d:koi with zaw, more: question word asking which of two) (b:koi) (q:draft)
kong = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:door/entrance/doorway) (d:the door or entrance of a house, tent or room) (s:kongkhak) (r:2.33.8)
kongkhak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:door/entrance/doorway) (d:the door of a house, tent or room, and the entrance it closes) (s:kong)
kote = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:we are/we/us) (d:first person plural pronoun that leaves out the person spoken to: ko with the plural te; English we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (s:ko/komau) (b:ko)
kua = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:who) (d:question word for a person: who; before a noun it asks whose, as in kua min, whose name) (r:1.3.11)
kuangdai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:plate/dish/platter) (d:a wide shallow dish, larger than kuang bowl) (s:dalkuang) (q:draft)
kul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:must/need/be necessary) (d:placed after a verb or after ding: it is necessary to, have to; with lo or se loin, there is no need to) (s:kisam) (r:5.18.22) (q:draft)
kum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:year) (d:a year, in counting time and in giving the age of a person; kum thum sung is for three years and kum za pha is be a hundred years old) (r:1.23.1)
la = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:song) (r:zai:song) (q:draft)
laam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:dance) (d:move the body to music, in joy or to entertain) (q:draft)
lai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone) (s:laikhak)
laikhak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone; laikhak sim is read a letter) (s:lai/laikhakna) (r:24.29.29) (q:draft)
laisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read/study) (d:lai, writing, with sim, read: read a text; laisim ngei lo is never having studied) (s:sim) (q:draft)
lak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take) (d:take something into the hand or into one's keeping. The form of la, take, used before endings and other words) (a:pia) (q:example wanted)
lampai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:walk/travel) (d:lam, road, and pai, go, also used as a noun, journey) (s:khualzin) (q:draft)
lampi = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:road) (b:lam)
lasa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:sing) (d:sing a song, from la, song, and sa, sing) (s:lasak) (q:draft)
lau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:afraid/frightened/fearful) (d:feeling fear; lau mahmah is very afraid) (s:meidawi) (a:hang/lungmuang)
lawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friend/companion) (d:a friend or companion; lawm ngaih is a lover or beloved) (s:lawmpa) (a:gal) (r:20.18.24) (q:draft)
lawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw/cast/hurl) (d:throw something or someone away from oneself, into or onto a place) (s:lot) (q:draft)
leengla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:guest/visitor) (d:often paired as zin le leengla, guests and strangers; zin le leengla do is to show hospitality) (s:zin/zinpa) (a:innteek) (q:draft)
leh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:joins words and phrases; also written le) (s:le)
leh = (i:3) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if/when) (d:placed after the verb of a clause to make it a condition; bang hang hiam cih leh, literally if one asks why, means because) (s:aleh/le) (r:1.4.15) (q:term added from the example, Genesis 4.15)
lei = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:buy) (r:zai:buy) (q:draft)
leitawi = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:borrow) (d:take something on loan, to be paid back later; said of what one does for another person it also means give on loan, lend) (q:draft)
leitawisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:lend) (d:leitawi, borrow, with the causative sak: let someone borrow, lend) (a:leitawi) (b:leitawi) (q:draft)
lel = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:lose/be defeated) (d:lose to an enemy or an opponent, the opposite of zo, win; gal lel is lose a war; the form lelh is used before some endings) (s:guallel/kizo) (a:zo/gualzo) (q:draft)
letsong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:gift/present) (d:something given to honor or please a person; letsong pia is give a gift) (s:piakkhong) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft)
leuleu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:again) (d:placed after a verb: once more, another time) (s:kik/kikkik)
lian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:large) (d:big in size) (s:gol/lianpi) (a:neu)
lo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not) (d:negative word placed after a verb or describing word: nei lo is not have, om lo is not be there)
lo = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:farm/field) (d:a piece of land that is worked to grow crops)
lokhopa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:farmer) (d:lokho, farm, with pa for a man: a man who works the land)
lui = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:old) (d:old, said of things, customs and times, the opposite of thak, new; hun lui is the days of old) (a:thak) (r:3.25.22) of objects which are just old
lukhu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:hat/cap) (r:zai:hat) (q:draft)
lum = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:warm) (d:warm; used with khua, the weather or how the body feels: khua lum is be warm, keep warm) (a:vot) (r:59.2.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungdam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:happy/glad/joyful) (d:glad or happy at heart, from lung, heart, and dam, well) (s:nuam)
lungdam = (i:4) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:thank you/thanks) (d:said to thank someone; the same word as lungdam, glad) (r:zai:thank) (q:draft)
lungdamkoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:thank/give thanks) (d:express thanks to someone, from lungdam, glad, and koh, express) (q:draft)
lupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:bed/couch) (d:a place to lie on and sleep, a bed) (s:lupphah) (q:draft)
lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:enter/go in) (d:go or come into a place; the place entered is usually marked with sungah, into, and the opposite is pusuak, go out) (s:sungtum) (a:pusuak/paikhiat) (r:40.12.9) (q:draft)
mahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:the very thing/very/indeed) (d:emphasises the word before it: after a describing word or verb it means very or indeed, after a noun the very one) (s:nakpi/nakpitakin)
makai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:leader/chief) (d:one who goes in front and is at the head of a tribe, a clan or a group of people) (s:makaipa/ukpi/ulian) (r:13.23.2) (q:draft)
man = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:finish/complete) (d:placed after another verb to say that the action is finished; a man khit ciangin means after finishing) (s:mankhit/zawhkhit) (a:kipan) (q:draft)
man = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:true/right/correct) (d:true or right, in agreement with the facts or with what ought to be; a man lo is false or wrong) (s:maan/mantak) (a:manlo) (q:draft)
man = (i:3) (t:n) (f:work) (w:price/value/cost/payment) (d:what is paid or owed for something: its price, its value or the payment for it; man pia is to pay) (s:manzah) (q:draft)
mangngilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:forget) (d:no longer remember, or fail to keep in mind; mangngilh kei is not forget) (a:phawk) (r:1.40.23) (q:draft)
mangpha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:goodbye/farewell) (d:the parting greeting; mangpha khak is to say goodbye, and mangpha kikhak to say goodbye to each other) (q:draft)
manin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:for/because/since) (d:placed at the end of a clause to give the reason for what follows; after a verb often ahih manin)
manlang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:quick/swift/fast/rapid) (d:quick or swift, said of feet, days or help; hong manlang in is come quickly, and manlang takin is rapidly)
manlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:false/untrue) (d:man, true, with lo, not: false, not true, said of words, witnesses and visions) (a:man/maan) (b:man) (q:draft)
mansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:lose) (d:have something go missing, lose it; mansuah hun is a time to give up as lost) (s:suplawh/taan) (q:draft)
mehteh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:vegetable/leaf vegetable/herbs) (d:leaf vegetables eaten as a cooked dish with the staple) (s:anteh) (q:draft)
mehtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:soup/broth) (d:meh, a cooked dish, with tui, water: the liquid of a stew, broth) (s:satui) (q:draft)
mei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/nature) (w:fire) (d:fire, the flame that burns; also a lamp or light, and the first part of many words such as meikuang, flame, and meikhu, smoke) (s:meikuang) (r:3.9.11) (q:draft)
meigong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:widow) (d:a woman whose husband has died, also said as meigong numei; often named together with pa nei lote, the fatherless) (s:meigongnu) (r:42.21.2)
melhoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:beautiful/handsome/good-looking) (d:of pleasing appearance, from mel, appearance, and hoih, good; said of women and of men) (s:meelhoih/ngaihbaang/etlawm) (a:melsia) (r:9.17.42) (q:draft)
melsia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:ugly/unsightly) (d:of unpleasant appearance, from mel, appearance, and sia, bad; the opposite of melhoih) (a:melhoih) (q:draft)
mi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:person/human being/people) (d:a human being, man or woman; with a number or quantity word it counts people, as in mi khat, one person, and mi tampi, many people) (s:mihing) (r:2.21.12)
mihon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:community/congregation/assembly/crowd) (d:mi, person, with hon, flock or group: a gathered body of people, a community, congregation or crowd) (s:mipi/honpi) (q:draft)
min = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:name)
minam = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social) (w:tribe/people/nation) (d:a people of one descent and language) (r:zai:tribe) (q:draft)
minit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:minute) (d:one of the sixty parts of an hour, a loanword from English) (r:zai:minute) (q:draft)
mipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:people/public/crowd/multitude) (d:mi, person, with the augmentative pi: the people as a body, the general public; mipi mai-ah is in public and mipi kikhopna is the great assembly) (s:mihonpi/mihon) (b:mi) (q:draft)
moh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:bread/cake/loaf) (d:a baked cake or loaf of bread) (r:28.7.8) (q:draft)
moi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:young) (d:young in age, the opposite of ham, old; a moi pen is the youngest, and a moi a ham is young and old alike) (s:khangno) (a:ham) (q:draft)
mopawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:wedding/wedding feast) (d:mo, bride, with pawi, feast: a wedding feast; mopawi sim is to attend a wedding) (s:molakpawi) (q:draft)
mu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:see) (d:perceive with the eyes) (r:1.1.4)
mu = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:saw/found/find) (d:come upon someone or something that was looked for or lost; maipha mu is to find favor) as in lost object discovered.
muak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:come to meet/seek out/welcome) (d:go out to meet or receive someone) (q:draft)
munphiah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:broom) (d:a tool for sweeping, compare phiat sweep) (q:draft)
na = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you/your) (d:second person marker: before a verb it means you, before a noun your) (s:nang) (r:2.20.3)
nai = (i:3) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/hour/o'clock) (d:an hour, or the hour of the day by the clock; nai khat is one hour and nitak nai thum is three in the afternoon)
nai = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:near/close) (d:near in place or time, not far) (r:zai:approach) (q:draft, low confidence)
nang = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you) (d:second person singular pronoun, used of one person; nang in marks the subject, and nang hong before a verb marks you as the object) (s:nangmah)
nangma = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:your) (d:possessive form of nang, placed before a noun; nangma aa is yours) (s:nangmah) (b:nang) (r:19.119.60)
nasem = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/serve) (d:do work, or serve an employer. From na, work, with sem, do, written as one word) (s:sem) (b:sem) (r:4.8.15) (q:draft)
nasep = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/job/service/duty) (d:the work a person does or is given to do: a task, a duty, an occupation; from na, work, and sep, do) (r:14.34.13)
nau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:child) (d:a baby or small child, also the child in the womb; nau paai is to be pregnant and nau suak to give birth) (s:naungek/naungeek)
naungek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:baby/infant) (d:a baby or very young child; nawi ne naungek is a baby still at the breast) (s:naungeek) (q:draft)
naupang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:child) (r:1.4.25) of offspring
nauzaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:younger one/younger sibling/the younger) (d:the younger of two children or siblings, opposite of uzaw the older) (b:nau) (q:draft)
nawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:milk) (d:milk, of a mother or of an animal such as a cow, sheep or goat; nawi ne is to drink milk, to nurse) (s:nawitui) (q:draft)
ne = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:eat) (d:take food; an ne is eat a meal; the form nek or neek is used before ding, theih and nading) (s:anne) (r:1.2.17)
neu = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:small) (d:not large in size, amount or importance; a neu a lian means small and great, everyone) (s:neuno) (a:lian/gol) as in appearance
nga = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:food/nature) (w:fish) (d:a fish, as a living creature and as food; the fuller word is ngasa) (s:ngasa)
ngai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:listen/pay attention) (d:give ear to what is said and take it to heart; ngai in is the command to one person and ngai un to several) (s:don/ngaihsak) (q:draft)
ngaih = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:loud) (d:loud, of a voice or sound, as in aw ngaih) (r:zai:loud) (q:draft)
ngaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think/consider/think about) (d:use the mind: think about something, consider it, or regard a person or thing in a certain way; ngaihsun un is the command to several people) (s:lungngai)
ngak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait/wait for/keep watch) (d:wait for someone or something, or stay awake and keep watch) (q:draft)
ngasa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:food/nature) (w:fish) (d:a fish, as a living creature and as food; ngasa bengte are fishermen) (s:nga)
ngeilo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never) (d:ngei, ever, with lo, not, placed after a verb: has never done or has never been so) (s:ngeikei/cikmah) (a:den/tawntunga) (b:ngei) (q:draft)
ngeina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:culture/tradition/custom/regulation) (d:the customary way of doing things, handed down from the ancestors; biakna ngeina is a fixed rule of worship) (b:ngei)
ngen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask for/request) (d:ask someone to give something; the form nget is used in dependent clauses) (q:draft)
ni = (i:1) (t:num) (f:time) (w:day) (d:a day as a length of time, used with a number to count days) (r:1.1.5) as in counting of days number
ni = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunt) (d:the sister of one's father) (r:zai:aunt) (q:draft)
niangtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tea) (d:tea as a drink) (r:zai:tea) (q:draft)
nin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:dirty/unclean) (d:dirty, not clean; the opposite of siang, clean) (s:nit/kihhuai) (a:siang/siangtho) (r:41.7.2) (q:draft)
nipikal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:week) (d:a period of seven days; nipikal khat is one week and nipikal sagih is seven weeks) (s:nisagih)
nitak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:evening) (d:the end of the day, from late afternoon until dark; nitak ciangin is in the evening, and nitak nai thum is three in the afternoon) (a:zingsang) (r:1.8.11)
nitak an = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food/time) (w:dinner/supper) (d:the evening meal) (r:zai:dinner) (q:draft)
not = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push/drive back/repulse) (d:push or force someone back; not kik is drive back and not zo is be able to repulse) (s:nawt)
note = (i:3) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you) (d:you, said to more than one person; with kiangah, to you, and with lakah, among you) (s:nomau) (b:no) (r:43.6.64/1.1.29) plural form of <no>
nu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:mother) (d:mother; a nu leh a pa is his mother and father) (a:pa) (r:41.3.33)
nu leh pa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:parent/parents) (d:mother and father, the parents of a person) (r:zai:parent) (q:draft)
nuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want) (d:want or be willing to do something, placed after the verb; with kei or lo, not want to) (s:deih/nop)
nuam = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:happy/glad/pleasant) (d:happy or glad; nuam mahmah is very glad, and lung nuam is glad at heart)
nui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laugh) (d:laugh, with joy or in disbelief; before another word such as hun, time, the form is nuih) (a:kap) (q:draft)
numei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:woman) (d:an adult female person) (a:pasal)
numeino = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girl/little girl/young girl) (d:numei, female, with no, young or small: a girl) (b:numei) (r:42.8.54) (q:draft)
nungak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:young woman/girl/maiden) (d:a young unmarried woman, a virgin) (a:tangval) (r:19.148.12) (q:draft)
nungciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:afterward/later/then) (d:nung, after, with ciangin, when; tua nungciangin is after that, a nungciangin is afterward or in turn) (s:nungcianga) (q:draft)
nungta = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:alive/live/be alive) (d:live, be alive; a nungta lai is still living) (a:si/sih) (r:27.6.21)
nuno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunt/mother's sister) (d:nu, mother, with no, young: the younger sister of one's mother) (b:nu) (q:draft)
om = (i:5) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:abide) (d:stay or live in a person or a place, remain there)
pa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:father) (d:male parent; with a possessive, as in ka pa, my father, and a pa, his father) (a:nu)
paai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw/cast/throw away) (d:throw, cast or throw away) (s:lawn/paii/lot) (r:43.10.11) (q:draft)
pai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go) (d:move from one place to another, go or walk to a place)
pai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come) (d:move toward the speaker or the place spoken of, usually with hong before it: hong pai, come here)
paikik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:pai, go or come, with kik, back or again: go back or come back to where one was; hong paikik is come back) (s:ciahkik/kilehkik) (b:pai) (q:draft)
paipih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:brought/bring/take/lead) (d:go taking a person or thing along: hong paipih is bring here, and paipih with a place is take or lead there) (b:pai) (r:1.2.22)
pano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:uncle) (d:uncle, the brother of the father; pa, father, with no, younger) (b:pa) (r:9.10.15) (q:draft)
panpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help/support/side with) (d:stand with someone, pan with pih together with; also join in with others and show partiality to) (s:pawlpih/pangkhawm/huh) (a:langpang) (b:pan) (r:20.23.11) (q:draft)
pasal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:man) (d:a man, an adult male person, as distinct from numei, a woman) (s:mipa) (a:numei)
pasal = (i:3) (t:n) (f:family) (w:husband) (d:a married man in relation to his wife) (r:zai:husband) (q:draft)
pasalno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:boy/male child) (d:pasal, male, with no, young) (s:naupangpa) (a:numeino) (b:pasal) (q:draft)
pau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:language/speech/word) (d:the language a people speaks, or what a person says; kam pau is speech or language, and pau lamdang is speaking in tongues) (s:kampau)
pau = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:speak/talk) (r:zai:say) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:festival/feast) (d:a feast or festival kept with eating and rejoicing; pawi bawl and pawi kham both mean hold a feast, and pawi hun is festival time) (s:pawikhamna) a day or period of celebration
pawlkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:a group/some) (d:pawl, group, with khat, one: one group; after a noun it means some of them) (s:honkhat)
pawlpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:church/congregation) (d:pawl, group, with pi, great: the church, the body of those who believe in Christ, or a local congregation) (b:pawl) (q:draft)
peeng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:twin) (d:one of two children or young animals born together at one birth) (r:44.28.11) (q:draft)
pha = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good) (d:good, the opposite of sia, bad or evil; a pha is what is good) (s:hoih) (a:gilo/hoihlo) (r:25.3.38) emotional feeling of being
phalbi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:winter/cold season) (d:the cold season of the year, winter, set against khuakhal, summer; phalbi lai is in winter) (s:phabi/phaibi) (a:khuakhal/khualkhal) (r:22.2.11) (q:draft)
phawk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remember) (d:keep or bring back in mind, the opposite of mangngilh, forget) (s:phawkkik/phawkkha) (a:mangngilh)
phazo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:enough/sufficient) (d:said of what is sufficient; phazo hi means that is enough, often said to stop someone)
pheek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:mat) (d:mat for lying on, in lupna pheek, sleeping mat) (q:draft)
phong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wake/awaken/rouse) (d:wake someone from sleep) (s:khanglosak/phawng) (q:draft)
phuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:name/call/give a name) (d:give a name to a child, a place or a thing, with min, name) (s:phuah)
phung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family/lineage) (d:the family line a person belongs to) (s:beh) (q:draft)
pi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandmother) (d:grandmother, the mother of one's father or mother) (q:draft)
pia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:hand something over to someone or grant it; thu pia is give an order and thupha pia is bless) (a:ngah/lak)
pu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandfather/forefather) (d:grandfather or forefather; pu pa and pu leh pate mean ancestors) (s:pupi/pulepa) (a:tupa) (r:14.29.2) (q:draft)
pua = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:carry/bear) (d:carry a load on the back or shoulder) (s:tawi) (r:5.31.25) (q:draft)
puak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/bring/deliver) (d:send or bring something to someone; thu puak is send word) (s:sawl) (q:draft)
puan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes/clothing/cloth) (d:cloth, or anything made of cloth to wear; many words for garments are built on it, such as puanak, puanpi and puanbuk) (s:nikten) (q:draft)
puanak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:shirt/coat) (d:garment worn on the upper body) (q:draft)
puanza = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:blanket) (d:a thick cloth to cover oneself with when sleeping) (r:zai:blanket) (q:draft)
puk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/fall down/stumble) (d:fall down or stumble, of people, animals and things) (s:tuk/kia) (a:tho) (q:draft)
sa = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:hot) (d:hot; a sa is the heat, the opposite of a vot, the cold) (a:vot)
sa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:meat) (d:the flesh of an animal as food; sa ne is eat meat and sa huan is cook meat) (s:sameh)
sabuai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:table) (d:a table, for eating at or for setting things on) (q:draft)
sam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/summon/invite) (d:call a person to come, call out to someone, invite; before a suffix the form is sap) (r:1.22.15)
san = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:red/scarlet) (d:the colour red, said of a horse, cloth, a cord, wine or the evening sky)
sang = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:high) (d:high above the ground or in position, said of mountains, clouds and the sun; the opposite of niam, low) (s:sangpi) (a:niam)
sang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:school) (s:sanginn)
sanggam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:brother/sister) (d:a brother or sister, a child of the same parents; sanggam pasal is a brother and sanggam numei a sister)
sanggamnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:sister) (d:sanggam brother or sister with nu, which marks a woman: a sister) (a:sanggampa) (b:sanggam)
sanggampa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:brother) (d:sanggam brother or sister with pa, which marks a man: a brother) (s:sangampa) (a:sanggamnu) (b:sanggam)
sangnaupang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:student/pupil) (d:sang school with naupang child) (q:draft)
sathau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/home) (w:oil) (d:oil or fat, used for cooking, for lamps and for rubbing on the body) (r:19.84.9) (q:draft)
satui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:soup/broth) (d:sa, meat, with tui, water: the liquid in which meat was boiled) (s:mehtui) (q:draft)
sau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:long) (d:long in measure or in time; after a number of cubits it gives the length) (s:saupi) (a:tom)
sawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send) (d:make someone go to a place or a person, with a task or a message) (s:puak/paisak) (r:55.4.12) (q:draft)
sawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push) (r:zai:push) (q:draft)
sawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:wash) (d:wash a thing or a part of the body such as clothes, nets, hands or feet) (s:sil) (r:42.5.2) (q:draft)
sawt = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:long/lasting) (d:long in time; a sawt loin is soon or before long, sawt pek is long ago, and sawt veipi is for a long time) (s:sau) (a:tom) (q:draft)
sawt lo-in = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:soon/before long) (r:zai:soon) (q:draft)
seeng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:basket) (d:a basket for carrying food or produce; also a basketful as a measure) (s:bawm/paipel) (q:draft)
sem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:work/operate/perform/serve/do) (d:do work or carry out a task; na sem is do work, and with a person named before it, serve that person) (a:tawlnga) (r:18.5.9)
si = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:die) (d:stop living; a si is he died and si lo is not die) (a:nungta)
sia = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:teacher/preacher) (d:one who teaches; sia leh a sinte is teacher and students) (s:siapa/thuhilhpa)
sia = (i:6) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:bad) (d:bad, not good, the opposite of pha and hoih) (r:zai:bad) (q:draft)
siang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:clean/pure) (d:clean, free from dirt; the opposite of nin, dirty) (s:siangtho) (a:nin/nit) (q:draft)
sikkeu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:spoon) (d:a spoon for eating; the row of the Bible lexicon has the sense fork) (r:zai:spoon) (q:draft)
sil = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body/home) (w:wash/bathe) (d:wash the body or a part of it, such as the hands and feet, with water) (s:sawp) (q:draft)
silh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:dress/clothe/wear/put on) (d:put on or wear clothes; puan silh is wear a garment) (s:puansilh) (a:suahkhia)
sim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:read) (d:read what is written, silently or aloud before others) (s:laisim) (q:draft)
sin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:learn/study) (d:gain knowledge or skill by study or by being taught; thu sin is learn a teaching) (q:draft)
singgah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:fruit) (d:sing, tree, with gah, fruit: the fruit of a tree; singgah kung is a fruit tree) (s:gah)
sinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:teach/instruct) (d:cause to learn; sin learn with the causative sak) (s:hilh/hilhsak/kisinsak) (b:sin) (q:draft)
sivuina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:funeral/burial) (r:zai:funeral) (q:draft)
sual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:floor) (d:the floor of a house or room; sual puan is a rug spread on the floor) (a:innsun) (r:26.41.16) (q:draft)
sum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:money/wealth) (d:money, and wealth counted in money; sum hau is be rich, sum leh pai is money and goods) (s:dangka/sumlepai) (q:draft)
sumbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:market/marketplace) (d:place of buying and selling; sumbuk vante is merchandise, sumbuk bawlte are traders) (s:sumzuakna/vanzuakna) (r:44.17.17) (q:draft)
sumlei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:buy) (d:buy with money, mostly in the pair sumlei sumzuak, buying and selling) (s:vanlei) (a:sumzuak) of currency
sun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:day/daytime) (d:the light part of the day, the opposite of zan, night; sun leh zan is day and night and sun-in is by day) (a:zan) as in during sun light
sunkim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:noon/midday) (d:the middle of the day; sunkim laipi is high noon) (s:suntang/suntangpi) (a:zankim) (r:11.18.29) (q:draft)
ta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:child) (d:a son or daughter, the child of someone; ta nei lo is childless)
taam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:stay/lodge/spend time) (d:stay somewhere for a time; zan taam means spend the night) (s:giak/zintun) (q:draft)
tagah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:orphan/fatherless child) (d:a child whose father or parents have died, often named together with meigong, widow; also used as a describing word, tagah tate fatherless children) (q:draft)
tai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:run/flee/run away) (d:run, and so run away or flee from danger or from a person; tai un is the command run or flee) (s:taikhia/taimang) (a:delh) (q:draft)
tam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:many) (d:large in number; a tam is the many, set against a tawm, the few, and tam mahmah is very many) (s:tampi) (a:tawm)
tampi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:numerous/many/much) (d:a large number or amount of something, placed after the noun: mi tampi is many people and thu tampi many things) (s:tam/tampite) (a:tawm/tawmno) (b:tam) quantity of being, plural form of <tam>
tamvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:many times/often/frequently) (d:tam many, with vei, time or occasion; tamvei zaw is more times) (s:tamveipi/zelzel) (q:draft)
tamzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:more/more numerous/greater) (d:comparative of tam, used with sangin for than) (a:tawmzaw) (b:tam) (q:draft)
tan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cut off/sever) (d:cut or break through, cut a thing in two) (s:sattan) (r:9.31.9) (q:draft)
tanau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:relative/kin/kinsman) (d:a member of one's own family or clan) (s:behpa/sanggam) (q:draft)
tangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:story/account) (d:an account of what happened, as in vantung leh leitung tangthu, the story of the heavens and the earth)
tangval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:boy/youth/young man) (d:a young unmarried man; tangval lai is still young) (a:nungak) of unmarried adult man
tanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:daughter) (d:a female child of her parents) (a:tapa)
tapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:son) (d:a male child of his parents; after a name, son of that person) (a:tanu)
taptung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:hearth/fireplace) (d:the place in the house where the cooking fire is kept) (r:zai:hearth) (q:draft)
tawh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (s:leh)
tawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/carry/bear) (d:hold or carry in the hand or arms) (s:len) (r:41.9.36) (q:draft)
tawlet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:window) (d:an opening in the wall of a house or ship for light and air; tawlet panin is from or through the window) (q:draft)
tawlnga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:rest) (d:stop working or moving in order to recover strength) (s:tawldam)
tawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:few/little/small) (d:small in number or amount; tawm khat is a little, a few, and tawm mahmah very few) (s:tawmno) (a:tam) (q:draft)
tawmzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:less/fewer/smaller/scarcer) (d:tawm, few, with zaw, more: fewer, less; sangin marks what it is compared with) (a:tamzaw) (b:tawm) (q:draft)
tawntung = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:continuously/nonstop/always/forever) (d:placed after a verb: going on without stopping or without end; uk tawntung is reign for ever) (s:paisuak)
teek = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:old/aged) (d:advanced in years, said of people; also as a verb, grow old) (s:ham/khangham) (a:khangno) (r:1.18.11) (q:draft)
tel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:understand/perceive) (d:grasp the meaning of what is heard or seen; tel lo is not understand, and tel thei is be able to understand) (s:theitel/theihtel) (q:draft)
tem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:knife/blade) (d:a knife or blade for cutting) (s:temta) (r:6.5.3) (q:draft)
temta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:knife/razor) (d:a knife; also a small knife for cutting a scroll and a razor for shaving) (s:tem) (b:tem) (q:draft)
teng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:live/dwell/settle) (d:have a home in a place or settle there; teng uh hi is they lived or settled) (s:teeng)
thahat = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:strong) (d:having strength of body or of faith; thahat un is the command be strong, and thahat lote are the weak) (s:hat/thakhauh) (a:thanem/thaneem)
thak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:new/fresh) (d:new, not old or used before, also fresh; placed after the noun, as in la thak, a new song) (a:lui) (r:42.5.38) (q:draft)
thanem = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:weak/feeble) (d:tha strength with nem soft: having little strength) (s:thaneem/zawngkhal) (a:thahat/hat) (r:23.16.14) (q:draft)
thei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know) (d:know a person, a fact or a way; thei kei is not know) (a:theilo)
thei = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:able/capable of/qualified to) (d:placed after a verb: able to do it, can; thei lo is unable) (a:theilo)
theitel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:understand/know fully/discern) (d:know a matter clearly and completely) (s:teltheih/tel) (q:draft)
thugen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:speak/say) (d:thu, word, with gen, say: speak to someone, address people; also used as a noun for what a person says) (s:gen)
thuk = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:food/everyday) (w:sour) (d:sour or acid in taste) (r:zai:acetic) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:agree/consent) (d:be of one mind about a matter, or accept what is asked or proposed, from thu, matter, and kim, complete) (s:kithutuak) (a:nial) (q:draft)
thuthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:news/new message/new thing) (d:thu, word or matter, with thak, new; thuthak hoih is good news) (s:thuzak/thupuak) (q:draft)
tom = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:short) (d:short in length, distance or time: lampi tom is a short road and hun tom a short time) (a:sau/sawt) (r:24.25.23) (q:draft)
tu = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:sit) (r:zai:sit) (q:draft)
tu = (i:3) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandchild) (d:the child of one's son or daughter) (r:zai:grandchild) (q:draft)
tu-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:now) (r:zai:now) (q:draft)
tua = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:that/those) (d:points to a person or thing already mentioned or known; before a noun it means that or those, and tua ciangin is then, after that) (a:hih) referring to a specific thing previously mentioned, known, or understood
tuam = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:different/separate/apart) (d:separate from the others or different from them: a tuam is separately, tuam om is live apart, nu tuam is of a different mother) (s:tuamdang) (a:kibang) (q:draft)
tuasan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:there/in that place) (d:tua, that, with san, place; used in tuasan takah, in that very place, there) (b:tua) (r:43.5.5) (q:draft)
tui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:water) (d:water, and any liquid; the first part of many compounds, such as tuikhuk, well, and tuipi, sea)
tuiduh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food/body) (w:thirsty) (d:tui, water, with duh, want: wanting water, thirsty; tuiduh mite are the thirsty) (s:dangtak) (b:duh)
tuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/fall down/stumble) (d:fall down or stumble. Of a thing, fall on something) (s:puk/kia) (a:tho/dingto) (r:19.37.24) (q:draft)
tum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:play/blow/sound) (d:play a musical instrument or sound a trumpet; the instrument stands before the verb, as peengkul tum, blow the trumpet) (s:mut) of instruments
tuni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:today) (d:this day, from tu, this, and ni, day; with the time marker in it means today, and tuni dongin is to this day)
tutak = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:now)
tutphah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:chair/seat/stool) (d:something to sit on, a chair, seat or stool) (s:tutna/tutphat) (q:draft)
u = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:older brother/older sister/elder sibling) (d:an older sibling of either sex; a u a nau, older and younger siblings, stands for brothers and sisters in general) (a:nau/nauzaw) (q:draft)
ui = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/home) (w:dog) (d:a dog, the animal kept at the house) (q:draft)
ukpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:chief/leader/head) (d:uk, rule, with pi, great: the head of a clan or tribe, a chief) (s:makai/makaipa/ukpipa) (b:uk) (q:draft)
upa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:elder/leader) (d:an elder or leader of a people, a town or a church; pawlpi upa is a church elder and upa vaihawmte are the ruling council) (s:makai) (r:64.1.1) (q:draft)
upa = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:elder/older/firstborn) (d:the older one among siblings; tapa upa pen is the eldest or firstborn son and ta upa zaw the older of two children) (s:uzaw) (a:khangnozaw) (q:draft)
vaimim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:maize/corn) (r:zai:maize) (q:draft)
vei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:time) (d:an occasion or instance, counted with a number word before it: khat vei is once, thum vei is three times)
vekpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all/altogether/in all) (d:the whole, everyone or everything together, used as a vekpi-in or a vekpi-un) (s:vekin/vekun) (q:draft)
veng = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:neighbourhood/neighbour/quarter) (d:the part of a village or town where one lives, and the people who live near) (s:veeng/innveng) (q:draft)
vok = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/food) (w:pig) (d:a pig; vok hon is a herd of pigs) (s:vokpi) (r:42.15.15)
vom = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:black/dark) (d:black or dark in colour, said of horses, hair, skin and the sky) (a:kang/paak) (q:draft)
vot = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:cold/cool) (d:cold or cool; a vot is the cold, the opposite of a sa, the heat) (s:khuavot) (a:sa/lum) (q:draft)
za = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:hear) (d:perceive sound, or learn of something by hearing; zak is the form used before ciangin and ding) (r:1.3.8)
zaang = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:light) (d:light in weight, not heavy) (r:zai:balsa) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:respect/honor) (d:show respect or honor to a person, such as parents, elders or rulers) (s:zaktak/pahtawi/zahtakbawl) (a:simmawh/zahko) (q:draft)
zahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:respect/honour/reverence) (d:the respect or honor shown to a person) (s:kihtakna/pahtawina) (a:simmawhna/zahkona) (b:zahtak) (q:draft)
zan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:night) (d:the dark part of the day, the opposite of sun, day; sun leh zan is day and night and zan khat is one night) (a:sun)
zankim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:midnight) (d:zan, night, with kim, half: the middle of the night; zankim lai takin is right at midnight) (a:sunkim)
zanni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:yesterday) (d:the day before today; with in, zanni-in, it tells when something happened) (q:draft)
zaw = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:than/more) (d:marks the comparative, more or rather; it follows the describing word, and the thing compared stands before it with sangin)
zawhngeu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/home) (w:cat) (r:zai:cat) (q:draft)
zawng = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:poor/needy) (d:having little money or property; also used as a verb, be poor or become poor) (s:cimawh/genthei) (a:hau) (q:draft)
zekai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be slow/be late/delay) (d:be late or slow in doing something, put it off; mostly with a negative, zekai lo, without delay) (a:kinawh) (r:10.20.5) (q:draft)
zelzel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:repeatedly/again and again/often) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action happens over and over) (s:zel/zeel/kikkik/tamvei) (r:18.33.29) (q:draft)
zi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:wife) (d:a married woman in relation to her husband; zi la or zi-in la is take a wife, marry) (a:pasal)
zin = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:guest/stranger/traveller) (d:one who is away from home, a guest in a house or a foreigner in a land; zin do is to show hospitality and zin tunna inn is a guest room or an inn) (s:khualmi/leengla/mikhual) (r:60.4.9) (q:draft)
zing an = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food/time) (w:breakfast) (d:the morning meal) (r:zai:breakfast) (q:draft)
zingciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:tomorrow/the next day) (d:also the day after an event: a zingciang ni) (a:zani) (q:draft)
zingsang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:morning) (d:the early part of the day; a zingsang ciangin is in the morning or the next morning, and zingsang tungin is early in the morning) (a:nitak)
zong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:also) (d:placed after the word or phrase it adds: this one as well as those already named)
zongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/but/yet/even if) (d:zong, also or even, with in: after a verb, although or even if; ahi zongin at the start of a clause is but or yet, and after each of several nouns it is whether or) (s:napi/hinapi)
zuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:sell) (d:give something to another person for money) (s:sumzuak) (a:sumlei) (q:draft)
